{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '6\\\\.3|6\\\\.4|6\\\\.5|P4′|8\\\\.1' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && rg --files src test | rg 'yang/(typescript|python/antlr|core/semantics)'\"","aggregated_output":"18:**Authority:** Subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md) (axioms, invariants, streams, host boundaries), [`adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md`](./adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md) (external effects as stream deposits), [`yang.antlr.md`](./yang.antlr.md) (§3 frontend SPI, §8.1–§8.2 semantic placement, §8.5.5 float addresses, §8.5.6 linked modules, §8.10 shared calling convention, §8.11 cells, §9 four-layer stdlib model), [`yang.typescript.md`](./yang.typescript.md) (§2.2 shared rulings, §17 lift enumeration, §19 owner decision A12.5), [`yang.php.md`](./yang.php.md) (§9 prelude inventory), [`yin.vm.linker.md`](./yin.vm.linker.md), [`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md), [`dao.jing.cbor.md`](./dao.jing.cbor.md), and [`src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md`](../../src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md).\n65:   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms carrying the §6.5 compilation derivation record (r8: frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor address, resolved runtime closure, input, output — reconciled by module symbol on every compilation, including a single lowerer revision paired with a conflicting runtime pin).\n98:   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\n99:   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, **`clj`**) in **both** bundled (`uast`) and linked (`module-uast`) emission, never exported and never exposed across `yrt.*`, Layer-2c libraries, or source scope.\n187:Remains unchanged at `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc` (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10): structural callable discovery (`entry`, `eligible?`), invocation records (`invocation`, `invocation-with`, `valid-invocation?`), and condition transfer (`condition`, `thrown`, `transfer`, `invoke`, `invoke-with`). Requires no `yrt.*` module so `yang.call` stays a leaf dependency.\n306:2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n336:### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n468:### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n483:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n554:### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n556:Under the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, all Clojure-family §8.10.7 callable/provenance bridging is unified directly into **trusted Layer-2b `clj`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`, requiring `yang.call` and `yrt.effect`) — eliminating both any separate `clj.bridge` module and `yang.clojure`'s legacy `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance code in P3:\n562:- **Full 4-step §8.10.7 entry boundary:**\n609:### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n646:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so the freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n650:| **P4′ — Additional N → 1 profiles** | `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1` next (descriptor + ts frontend contract); `:yang.php/clojure-core-v1` after. | Fresh goldens per profile | End-to-end parity suites per profile. |\ntest/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/global_write_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/scope_test.clj\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/string_forms_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/corpus_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/float_address_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/class_prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/cst_test.clj\ntest/yan