{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc; sed -n '2230,2410p' src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc; tail -145 src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.frontends\n  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure frontend and the ANTLR PHP and\n   Python frontends installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n\n   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n   already read, else the source text.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    #?@(:cljd []\n        :jolt []\n        :default [[yang.php.antlr.cst :as php.antlr.cst]\n                  [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php.antlr.lower]])\n    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-runtime]\n    [yang.python.antlr.contract :as python.contract]\n    [yang.python.antlr.profiles :as python.profiles]\n    [yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.repl]\n    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.parser]\n    [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.probe]\n    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n\n\n(defn- manifest\n  [id language]\n  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n   :yang.frontend/language language,\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n\n\n(defn clojure-manifest\n  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it.\n   Revision c1-2 additionally declares the constructed-collections\n   lowering profile: a dynamically constructed map or set literal now\n   orders its constructor operands by compiled content\n   (:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1), a one-time canonical\n   shift for affected newly compiled artifacts; the C1 support claim,\n   the C1 marker value and the execution grammar versions are\n   unchanged.\"\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-2\"\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n\n\n(defn- clojure-lower\n  [forms]\n  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n\n\n(defn- antlr-manifest\n  [id {:keys [descriptor-address runtime-address]}]\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n         :yang.frontend/revision (name id)\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile descriptor-address\n         :yang.frontend/runtime-profile runtime-address\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile descriptor-address\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n\n\n(defn php-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/php :php)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"antlr-p8\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"php\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"htmlDocument\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript}}\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.php/antlr\n         :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :yang.php/antlr\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.php/antlr))\n\n\n(defn- parse-python [source]\n  #?(:jolt\n     (try (python.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))\n          (catch Exception e\n            (if (#{:parser-budget :unavailable-parser} (:diagnostic (ex-data e)))\n              (throw (ex-info (ex-message e) (assoc (ex-data e) :lang :yang/python) e))\n              (throw e))))\n     :default (python.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))))\n\n\n(defn- install-python [catalog id]\n  (let [profile (python.profiles/builtin id)\n        manifest (antlr-manifest id profile)\n        legacy? (= id python.contract/legacy-id)\n        lower (if legacy? python.repl/lower-session python.repl/lower-clojure-session)\n        lower-session (fn [packet session]\n                        (python.profiles/verify-builtin! id)\n                        (lower packet session (:descriptor profile)))]\n    (frontend/install catalog manifest\n      (cond-> {:parse (fn [source]\n                         (python.profiles/verify-builtin! id)\n                         (parse-python source))\n               :lower (fn [packet] (first (lower-session packet nil)))\n               :lower-session lower-session\n               :derive (fn [packet ast] (python.profiles/derivation manifest profile packet ast))\n               :probe (fn [source]\n                        (python.profiles/verify-builtin! id)\n                        (python.probe/probe source))\n               :render (if legacy? python.repl/display-value python.repl/display-clojure-value)}\n        legacy? (assoc :primitives python.repl/primitives)\n        (not legacy?) (assoc :admit clj-runtime/admit)))))\n\n\n(defn standard\n  \"The standard immutable frontend catalog and the preferred Python revision.\"\n  []\n  (let [catalog (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n                  true (frontend/install (clojure-manifest)\n                                         {:input :forms :parse identity :lower clojure-lower})\n                  #?@(:cljd []\n                      :jolt []\n                      :default [true (frontend/install\n                                       (php-manifest)\n                                       {:parse php.antlr.cst/parse-source\n                                        :lower php.antlr.lower/lower-packet\n                                        :render :php/out})]))]\n    (if #?(:jolt (python.parser/available?) :default true)\n      (-> catalog\n          (install-python python.contract/legacy-id)\n          (install-python python.contract/clojure-id)\n          (assoc :yang.frontend/preferred [:yang/python \"clojure-core-v1\"]))\n      catalog)))\n\n(defn create-state\n  \"`yin.repl/create-state` composed with the standard catalog unless the\n   host supplies its own `:frontends`.  Each binding registers its own\n   `:primitives`; none is merged ambiently.\"\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (repl/create-state (update opts :frontends #(or % (standard))))))\n;; Packets\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- context\n  [packet]\n  (let [pk (p/validate! packet {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns})\n        analysis (scope/analyze pk)]\n    {:pk pk,\n     :analysis analysis,\n     :scope (:module analysis),\n     :this (gen \"this\" (p/root pk)),\n     :ret nil,\n     :loop nil,\n     :labels {},\n     :pending-labels nil,\n     :gen nil,\n     :async nil,\n     :class nil,\n     :this-cell nil,\n     :nt :undefined,\n     :home nil,\n     :class-cell nil,\n     :privates {}}))\n\n\n(defn- module-body\n  [ctx]\n  (let [root (p/root (:pk ctx))\n        s (scope-of ctx root)\n        stmts (statements-of ctx root)]\n    (bind-cells (let [{:keys [vars tdz-names]} (binding-names s)]\n                  (vec (concat (map (fn [nm] [nm undefined]) vars)\n                               (map (fn [nm] [nm tdz]) tdz-names))))\n                (seq-of (lower-stmts ctx stmts)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a tree this namespace answers\n;; carries the reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with\n;; version value `1` as a plain node key. Projection\n;; (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key from canonical rows and emits\n;; it into the EXISTING generic frontend-metadata side table as\n;; `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, so provenance stays out\n;; of hashed content: canonical rows, roots, image addresses and\n;; executable outcomes are unchanged. The walk itself is\n;; `yang.core.uast/annotate-call-sites`; nothing here re-mints the key or\n;; the coordinate tuple. It is a distinct key from `:yang/site`, the\n;; safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata, and a distinct key\n;; FAMILY again from the exception track's runtime provenance doors\n;; `cell/dsg__new-provenance` / `cell/dsg__provenance`.\n;;\n;; Coverage is all-or-nothing: `yin.vm.encoder/program-batch` and\n;; `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` each refuse a tree whose\n;; markers do not exactly cover its eligible application occurrences. So\n;; each PUBLIC entry point below finalizes once, over its own complete\n;; tree, after canonical renaming and tail marking have settled it — and\n;; the private `lower-unit*` seam exists so `lower-units` and\n;; `lower-packet` compose unmarked units and walk the composed result a\n;; single time, rather than leaving their own wrapper applications\n;; (`js/run-main`, the two `require`s, `js/init!`, the sequencing lambdas)\n;; unclaimed beside a marked unit.\n\n(defn lower-module-body\n  \"The module's statements as one node, before the runtime wrapper: what\n   lowering goldens compare. C1 finalized, like every tree this namespace\n   answers.\"\n  [packet]\n  (u/annotate-call-sites (module-body (context packet))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-unit*\n  \"`lower-unit` before C1 finalization: the seam `lower-units` and\n   `lower-packet` compose, so each of them finalizes once over its own\n   complete tree.\"\n  [packet]\n  (let [ctx (context packet)]\n    (u/lam [(:this ctx)] (module-body ctx))))\n\n\n(defn lower-unit\n  \"One separately scoped module body as a function of its shared global\n   receiver. Keeping this seam lets a host compose independently parsed\n   units without concatenating source or reinitializing the runtime.\n   C1 finalized.\"\n  [packet]\n  (u/annotate-call-sites (lower-unit* packet)))\n\n\n(defn- with-runtime\n  \"Both source entry points install the shared convention before JS.\"\n  [prelude main]\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (case prelude\n      :bundled (u/then prelude/uast main)\n      :linked (u/seq-nodes [(app* 'require (u/lit 'yang.call))\n                            (app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))\n                            (app* 'js/init!)\n                            main]))))\n\n\n(defn lower-units\n  \"A complete program for multiple separately parsed units. The runtime is\n   installed and initialized once; each unit receives its own lexical body\n   while sharing the same global object and output stream. C1 finalized\n   once, over the composed tree.\"\n  ([packets] (lower-units packets {}))\n  ([packets {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n   (let [units (mapv lower-unit* packets)\n         main (names/canonicalize\n                (app* 'js/run-main\n                      (u/lam ['this]\n                             (if (seq units)\n                               (u/seq-nodes\n                                 (mapv (fn [unit] (u/app unit (u/v 'this))) units))\n                               (u/lit :js/undefined)))))]\n     (u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main)))))\n\n\n(defn lower-packet\n  \"The complete program for one ok packet: the module body run by\n   `js/run-main`, generated names canonicalized, tail calls marked, C1\n   finalized. Its value is `{:js/out [...] :js/uncaught nil-or-snapshot}`.\n\n   `:prelude` selects how the runtime profile arrives: `:bundled` (the\n   default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked` requires\n   the modules `yang.call` and `js` from the task's link pair, then allocates\n   the task's runtime state with `(js/init!)`.\"\n  ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n  ([packet {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n   (let [main (names/canonicalize (app* 'js/run-main (lower-unit* packet)))]\n     (u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main)))))\n\n\n(def program-medium\n  \"The program medium's logical identity when the composition names none.\"\n  :yang.ts/program)\n\n\n(def ^:private stage-config\n  {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns,\n   :program-medium program-medium,\n   :ok? #(= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome %)),\n   :lower (fn [state packet]\n            (lower-packet packet {:prelude (get state :prelude :bundled)})),\n   :option-keys [:prelude :dialect]})\n\n\n(defn lower-transform\n  \"The lowering stage's transform (`yang.core.stage/lower-transform`).\"\n  [state packet]\n  (core-stage/lower-transform stage-config state packet))\n\n\n(defn open-stage\n  \"A lowering stage reading CST packets from `cst-stream`, writing program\n   batches to `program-stream`, whose logical identity is `medium`, and\n   diagnostics to `diagnostics-stream`. The fourth argument may instead be\n   an options map `{:medium :prelude :dialect}`.\"\n  ([cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream]\n   (core-stage/open-stage stage-config\n                          cst-stream\n                          program-stream\n                          diagnostics-stream))\n  ([cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream medium-or-opts]\n   (core-stage/open-stage stage-config\n                          cst-stream\n                          program-stream\n                          diagnostics-stream\n                          medium-or-opts)))\n\n\n(defn step-stage\n  [s]\n  (core-stage/step-stage stage-config s))\n         (js/throw-type-error {:js/str \"Spread value is not iterable\"})))]])\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order:\n   every prelude function, the literal state slot, then `js/init!`.\n   Defining them runs nothing.\"\n  (into (into (into (into (into (into core-definitions object-definitions)\n                                t4-definitions)\n                          array-definitions)\n                    json-definitions)\n              class-definitions)\n        [['js.rt/state :js/uninit] ['js/init! (init-form)]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private linked-definitions\n  \"The `js` module body; the common call runtime is pinned as a requirement.\"\n  definitions)\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  (core/balanced-definitions->uast defs))\n\n\n(def functions-uast\n  \"The shared calling runtime followed by every js definition. Defining\n   them runs nothing, so this loads on any composition, with or without cells.\"\n  (definitions->uast (into call/definitions definitions)))\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled prelude: every definition, then the task's runtime state\n   allocated by `js/init!`.\"\n  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(js/init!))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The linked js module requires the separately published `yang.call` module\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module the JavaScript runtime profile is published as.\"\n  'js)\n\n\n(def runtime-keys\n  \"Every key `js/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted.\"\n  (vec (sort-by str\n                (concat '[js.rt/ctx js.rt/out js.rt/global js.rt/obj-proto\n                          js.rt/fn-proto js.rt/symbol-proto js.rt/array-proto]\n                        (map second error-classes)\n                        (map first primitive-protos)))))\n\n\n(defn strip\n  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `js`; any other value as it\n   is. `js.rt/*` stays qualified: an internal store key.\"\n  [sym]\n  (core/strip \"js\" sym))\n\n\n(def ^:private module-definitions\n  \"The module's definition list: a `:js/uninit` placeholder for every\n   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n  (core/module-definitions \"js\" :js/uninit runtime-keys linked-definitions))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  \"The module tree: one application whose operands are the definitions, in\n   order, applied to a lambda that returns nil. C1 finalized, like every\n   published production tree: its `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside\n   its manifest (see `yin.vm.linker.publish`), never inside it, so the\n   manifest keeps schema 1 and its address does not move.\"\n  (u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The module's exports: every `js/` key of the definition list, stripped.\"\n  (core/exports \"js\" definitions))\n\n\n(def free-names\n  \"Every variable name some occurrence of the map AST reads unbound by an\n   enclosing lambda.\"\n  core/free-names)\n\n\n(def defined-keys\n  \"Every literal key the map AST defines with `yin/def`, at any depth.\"\n  core/defined-keys)\n\n\n(def ^:private module-free-names\n  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the\n   primitives and the host exports its manifest must declare.\"\n  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `js` over\n   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call` module\n   at `call-address`. A free name nothing supplies is refused before\n   anything is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  [registry call-address]\n  (prelude-admission/module-spec\n    {:module-name module-name,\n     :ast module-uast,\n     :exports module-exports,\n     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n     :free-names module-free-names,\n     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n     :registry registry,\n     :message \"the js module reads an undeclared name\",\n     :refusal-ns \"yang.typescript.antlr\"}))\n\n\n(def min-integer-bits\n  \"The smallest `::integer/max-bits` this profile admits: every inline\n   literal (up to 2^53 - 1) must fit.\"\n  53)\n\n\n(defn register-integer-module\n  \"Return `registry` with the `integer` module installed under `limits`\n   for this profile: refused when `::integer/max-bits` is under\n   `min-integer-bits`, otherwise `integer/register-integer-module`.\"\n  [registry limits]\n  (let [b (::integer/max-bits limits)]\n    (when-not (and (int? b) (<= min-integer-bits b))\n      (throw (ex-info \"the JavaScript profile needs integer max-bits >= 53\"\n                      {:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal\n                       :yang.typescript.antlr/max-bits,\n                       ::integer/max-bits b}))))\n  (integer/register-integer-module registry limits))\n\n\n(defn admit\n  \"Return `registry` when it supplies every one of `host-names`, else\n   refuse it before any program runs, naming each missing export in\n   `:yang.typescript.antlr/missing`.\"\n  [registry]\n  (prelude-admission/admit registry host-names\n                           \"the composition lacks host names the prelude calls\"\n                           \"yang.typescript.antlr\"))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
