{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_164","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented P4′-a on `feat/p4-ts-clojure-core`. The work is uncommitted at `0c36043d`, and all six new files are marked intent-to-add.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- [profiles.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/profiles.cljc) pins and admits both TypeScript revisions through the shared descriptor validator. [contract.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/contract.cljc:93) records the hook arities, address-bound roles, and both entry shapes.\n- [lower.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc:2566) reads literals, hooks, capabilities, and projections from the descriptor. [clj_runtime.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/clj_runtime.cljc) delegates callable creation and invocation to `clj` and installs the cold-error policy for each unit.\n- The [TypeScript frontend binding](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/frontend.cljc), [shared selector](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:193), and [REPL catalog](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:135) select `clojure-core-v1` for ordinary TypeScript requests, retain explicit `ts-v1` selection, and preserve in-flight selections.\n- The [TypeScript suite](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/test/yang/typescript/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc) and [portable CST fixtures](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/test/resources/yang/typescript/clojure_core_packets.edn) cover eight bundled and linked roots, numeric semantics, key admission, equivalence, canonical ordering, rendering, exceptions, and structured refusals.\n\nThe [Python composition-swap fixture](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/test/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:381) redirects `identity` from `clojure.core` to the already-admitted `clj.py/ex-info`. The modified descriptor executes in bundled and linked modes, and provenance records the updated descriptor and resolver addresses and the `clj.py` address in the runtime closure. The same swap without the exact projection-role grant fails closed. All 13 swap assertions passed on JVM and Node.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.typescript.antlr.descriptor-profile-test` | **Pass**, 6 tests, 226 assertions |\n| `node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.typescript.antlr.descriptor-profile-test` | **Pass**, 4 tests, 175 assertions |\n| `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.typescript.antlr.descriptor-profile-test` | **Pass**, 4 tests |\n| `\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test build/p4-jolt-execution-probe.clj` | **Pass**, 2 assertions for the bundled numeric root and register VM result. A separate probe verified both descriptor and runtime pins. |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.descriptor-profile-test` and `node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.python.antlr.descriptor-profile-test` | Each ran 12 tests and 119 assertions, with zero failures and three inherited `py-v1` pin errors. The pin mismatch reproduces at `0c36043d`. |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test -n yang.typescript.antlr.float-address-test -n yang.typescript.antlr.prelude-module-test` | **Pass**, 18 tests, 74 assertions |\n| `node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test,yang.typescript.antlr.float-address-test,yang.typescript.antlr.prelude-module-test` | **Pass**, 18 tests, 74 assertions |\n| `clojure -M build/p4-native-lowering-parity.clj` | **Pass**, 736 identical native UASTs or refusals against `0c36043d`, covering T1–T3 and the multi-unit fixtures in both modes |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.frontend-test` and `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` | **Pass**, 3 tests and 29 assertions for the selector, with zero dependency cycles or multi-node SCCs |\n\n**The full slow native oracle execution gate remains open.** The untouched sweeps entered 153 JVM and 26 Node corpus cases without a reported mismatch before I stopped the local suite-scale runs. The build guide assigns those runs to remote test hosts. The combined Jolt namespace run was also stopped before it reported suite totals. [Build and test guide](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/docs/agents/build-n-test.md:196)\n\n## Design rulings applied\n\n- §6.4(6) specifies the native “js single-operand” entry. `ts-v1` keeps `js/run-main [body]`, and `clojure-core-v1` uses `clj.ts/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]`.\n- §6.5 puts the “preferred `[frontend-id revision]` pair” in the composition. The catalog selects Clojure semantics by default, and bare compiler calls retain the native pin used by the existing oracles.\n- §6.3’s projection table maps to legal TypeScript aliases such as `assocIn`, `isNil`, and `exInfo`. The profile uses boxed float64 for TypeScript `Number` literals and exact integers for `BigInt` literals. It admits named imports from projected ambient modules. [Governing design](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4ts/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:336)"}}
